// DF-174d, second half. A bare unknown name is indistinguishable from a type
// parameter or an associated type at resolution time, so an unknown one used to
// become an opaque nominal and report a MISMATCH against it — a type with no
// declaration, no members and no explanation.
//
// Type ARGUMENTS were what settled the question first: a type parameter takes
// none and neither does an associated type, so a name carrying them and
// resolving to nothing is a name the program does not define. Design 241 unit 1
// settled the BARE shape too, by asking the question where the type parameters
// in force are known, and retired this rule's separate implementation — so the
// wording here is the funnel's, anchored on the name rather than on the `let`.
// See unknown_type_name_diagnostic.saw for the whole position matrix.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: undefined type `Frobnicate`

func main() {
    let a: Frobnicate<Int> = 5
    print("{a}")
}
